---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import ProductGrid from '../../components/ProductGrid.astro';
import FAQAccordion from '../../components/FAQAccordion.astro';
import QuoteForm from '../../components/quote/QuoteForm.tsx';
import { serviceSchema } from '../../lib/schema/service';
import { faqPageSchema } from '../../lib/schema/faqPage';
import { getAllProducts } from '../../data/catalog/shopify';
import '../../styles/quote-form.css';

const allProducts = await getAllProducts();
const products = allProducts.filter((p) => p.tags.includes('wall') || p.tags.includes('backdrop')).slice(0, 9);

const faqs = (await getCollection('faq'))
  .filter((f) => f.data.pages.includes('walls'))
  .sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order)
  .map((f) => ({ question: f.data.question, body: f.body.trim() }));

const schemas = [
  serviceSchema({
    name: 'Balloon walls and backdrops',
    description:
      'Custom balloon walls and photo backdrops built to venue dimensions and installed for events in London Ontario.',
    startingPrice: 200,
    url: '/services/walls-backdrops',
  }),
];
if (faqs.length > 0) {
  schemas.push(faqPageSchema(faqs.map((f) => ({ question: f.question, answer: f.body }))));
}
---

<BaseLayout
  topic="Balloon Walls and Backdrops"
  description="Custom balloon backdrops and walls in London Ontario. Built to your dimensions and palette, delivered and installed. Accent walls from $200, full feature walls to $1,750."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Services', url: '/services' },
    { name: 'Walls and backdrops', url: '/services/walls-backdrops' },
  ]}
  schemas={schemas}
>
  <Hero
    eyebrow="Install type"
    headline="Balloon backdrops and walls in London, Ontario"
    subhead="Photo-ready focal points sized to your venue and your photographer's frame. Any palette, built to order, installed by us."
    primaryCta={{ href: '/quote', label: 'Start a quote' }}
    secondaryCta={{ href: '/portfolio', label: 'See backdrop work' }}
    image="/images/categories/BalloonHeartWall.webp"
    imageAlt="Heart-shaped balloon wall backdrop"
    variant="page"
  />

  <section class="install-body section">
    <div class="container container-narrow prose">
      <p>
        A balloon backdrop does the job a banner cannot. It gives the photo depth, colour, and texture,
        and it keeps working all night because every guest ends up standing in front of it at some
        point. It is the piece that shows up in the most photos afterward, which is why it is worth
        sizing properly rather than ordering by price alone.
      </p>

      <h2>What a balloon backdrop costs in London</h2>
      <p>
        Accent walls and half-height backdrops start around $200. A standard photo backdrop, the eight
        by eight foot size most events want, runs $349 to $699. Full feature walls that span a room,
        include a neon sign or name cutout, or carry floral and greenery inserts land between $699 and
        $1,750.
      </p>
      <p>
        Three things move that number. Coverage is the biggest one, because a densely packed wall uses
        several times the balloons of an organic wall of the same dimensions. Colour count is next,
        since every added colour is a separate inflation batch before Brenda starts building. Then the
        surface, because a freestanding frame is a different build from something anchored to a wall,
        and some venues will not let anything touch their walls at all.
      </p>

      <h2>Getting the size right</h2>
      <p>
        Most people undersize a backdrop. Eight feet wide by eight tall covers one or two people
        comfortably. Group shots need ten to twelve feet wide, because a row of six guests takes up
        more room than it looks like it will, and a backdrop that stops behind someone's shoulder is
        the thing you notice in every photo later. Height matters more than width once people are
        standing, and anything under seven feet tall starts showing the ceiling behind it at eye level.
        Send a photo of the wall or corner you have in mind and we will tell you what actually fits.
      </p>

      <h2>Branded walls for corporate events</h2>
      <p>
        For grand openings, brand activations, and conference booths around London and southwestern
        Ontario, we build to a brand palette rather than a stock colour set. That means matching your
        specific colours instead of picking the closest standard shade, and working a logo, name, or
        hashtag into the wall as a cutout or sign. Step-and-repeat style walls for media photos work
        the same way. If you are coordinating this alongside other vendors, Brenda deals with the venue
        on load-in timing directly. See the <a href="/services/corporate">corporate packages</a> page
        for how the rest of that fits together.
      </p>

      <h2>Related install types</h2>
      <p>
        A backdrop framing a doorway or an entrance is usually a
        <a href="/services/balloon-arches">balloon arch</a> instead. Something running along a wall,
        rail, or head table is a <a href="/services/balloon-garlands">balloon garland</a>. Many setups
        combine a wall with a garland trailing off one corner, which reads bigger than either on its
        own. Pricing and timelines for all of it are in the <a href="/faq">FAQ</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {products.length > 0 && (
    <section class="install-products section">
      <div class="container">
        <header class="section-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">Shop the catalog</p>
          <h2>Walls and backdrops in the catalog</h2>
          <p class="lede">Pick a build as-is or use it as the base for a custom version.</p>
        </header>
        <ProductGrid products={products} columns={3} />
        <p class="section-link-wrap">
          <a class="section-link" href="https://shop.balloonia.events/collections/walls-backdrops">View all walls and backdrops →</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  )}

  {faqs.length > 0 && <FAQAccordion heading="Balloon backdrop questions" faqs={faqs} />}

  <section class="install-quote section">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Custom build</p>
        <h2>Want a custom wall?</h2>
        <p class="lede">Send your dimensions, palette, and any references. Brenda quotes within 24 hours.</p>
      </header>
      <QuoteForm client:load />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose p { color: var(--color-ink-soft); font-size: var(--font-size-lg); line-height: var(--line-relaxed); }
  .prose h2 { margin-top: var(--space-6); margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
  .prose a { color: var(--color-accent-deep); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 4px; }
  .section-head { margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }
  .install-quote { background: var(--color-paper-soft); }
  .section-link { color: var(--color-accent-deep); font-size: var(--font-size-sm); font-weight: 500; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 4px; }
  .section-link-wrap { margin-top: var(--space-5); }
</style>
